planning-mds/examples/README.md:113:From the repository root, run `python3 scripts/validation/validate_semantic_examples.py`. It validates the educational JSON against its local schema and checks record and planning references. Reviewers still judge the meaning, the accuracy of expected outcomes, and completeness of concept coverage. The product checklist makes that review explicit.
planning-mds/domain/glossary.md:7:This glossary keeps the semantic kernel vocabulary and the insurance vocabulary consistent across requirements, architecture, code, and the knowledge graph, and lets agents understand domain concepts without inventing definitions.
planning-mds/domain/glossary.md:17:**Definition:** The top of the structural tenancy hierarchy (Tenant → Workspace → KnowledgeBase); every authoritative semantic row carries `tenant_id` (65, ADR-0030)
planning-mds/domain/glossary.md:76:**Definition:** The canonical semantic identity of one fact about an entity, for example the EachOccurrence limit of a coverage; the unit that fact versions attach to (13, ADR-0006)
planning-mds/domain/glossary.md:97:**Definition:** An accepted value for a FactSlot carrying both a valid-time period and a recorded-time period, with change semantics when it ends (14, 16, ADR-0007, ADR-0009)
planning-mds/domain/glossary.md:228:**Definition:** Each document version is physically parsed exactly once; all later semantic work operates on the persisted content artifact (5, ADR-0003)
planning-mds/domain/glossary.md:299:| Ontology module version | Immutable revision of one module with its definitions, semantics, constraints, and dependency declarations | [EX-ONT-005](../examples/ontology-release-contracts.md#composed-releases-and-packages): GL version 2 declares its foundation dependency | F0012/F0013, v0.1A |
planning-mds/domain/glossary.md:408:These terms refine representation and admission under [ADR-0075](../architecture/decisions/ADR-0075-versioned-assertion-semantics-and-admission.md); Phase B design was approved by operator on 2026-11-01; runtime proofs remain pending. All examples are synthetic and illustrative in [EX-ASSERT-001–009](../features/archive/F0006-assertion-plane-origin-and-interpretation-basis/worked-examples.md).
planning-mds/domain/glossary.md:412:| Assertion semantic extension | Immutable version-2 representation keyed to the existing assertion identity, retaining typed/open kind, independent mode/origin/basis, source wording and server-verified evidence | EX-ASSERT-001/003/009: preserve two claims and old raw history; never backfill a missing quote or ontology release | F0006 S0001/S0002/S0005; assertion-record-v2, interpretation-result-v2 |
planning-mds/domain/glossary.md:420:These are proposed retrieval design terms for v0.2A F0033–F0036, with optional numerical derivatives in v0.4+ F0068. Definitions follow [ADR-0076](../architecture/decisions/ADR-0076-governed-graph-assisted-evidence-retrieval.md); examples and boundary cases are [EX-RET-001–006](../examples/governed-evidence-retrieval.md). They do not alter canonical fact, assertion or permission semantics.
planning-mds/domain/glossary.md:432:The pinned semantic snapshot, both temporal coordinates/precision, ontology, root/requested scope, knowledge mode, current-authorization decision reference, actual projection versions, retrieval profile/effective mode and model/tokenizer profile for one retrieval. Recorded authority is not a reusable access grant (EX-RET-003/004/006; F0035/F0036).
